1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,300
In films,

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,440
quicksand swallows people whole.

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:03,900
Physics says

4
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,314
you'd stop at your waist.

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,240
Quicksand is fine sand,

6
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,720
clay and salt water.

7
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,380
Leave it alone,

8
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,931
and it slowly thickens.

9
00:00:12,931 --> 00:00:13,560
Step on it,

10
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,160
and it turns to liquid.

11
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,460
The harder you push,

12
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:17,611
the runnier it gets.

13
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:19,220
So you sink.

14
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,100
And thrashing

15
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,502
makes you sink faster.

16
00:00:22,602 --> 00:00:24,100
But here's the catch.

17
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:24,940
Quicksand is about

18
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,763
twice as dense as you are.

19
00:00:27,763 --> 00:00:28,760
So you float.

20
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,480
You sink to about your waist.

21
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,369
Then you stop.

22
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:33,240
In the lab,

23
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,960
a ball as dense as a person

24
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,360
would not go under.

25
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,883
However hard they shook it.

26
00:00:38,983 --> 00:00:39,440
Getting out

27
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,780
is the hard part.

28
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,980
Around your legs,

29
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:43,578
the sand packs down tight.

30
00:00:44,578 --> 00:00:45,820
The researchers' estimate:

31
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,300
pulling one foot out,

32
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,120
at 1 cm a second,

33
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,440
takes about the force

34
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,944
needed to lift a car.

35
00:00:53,044 --> 00:00:54,200
So don't let your friends

36
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,120
yank you out.

37
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,800
One of the physicists warned

38
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,900
they could pull you

39
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,122
into 2 pieces.

40
00:01:00,222 --> 00:01:00,720
Instead,

41
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:02,780
wiggle your legs slowly.

42
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:03,720
Water trickles down

43
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:05,280
and loosens the sand.

44
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:05,920
Lie back,

45
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,881
and let your legs float free.

46
00:01:08,881 --> 00:01:09,720
The real risk

47
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:11,100
isn't the sand.

48
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:11,900
It's being stuck

49
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:12,640
near the sea

50
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,072
when the tide comes in.

51
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,100
Quicksand doesn't

52
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:16,980
swallow you.

53
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,128
It just holds on.

